From a6217b8a1f34d3f32fd49045bd61b1663bbe0a8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:41:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wp_vehicle, simcli: ground-probe tilt fix (tyre-load chatter
 in corners) + [bless] 64 goldens and the slide_control wheel-profile hashes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In a steady corner every tyre's load jumped 0.6–1.0 kN RMS from tick to tick (zero when
straight): the body-fixed probe cylinder's edge reaches a flat road ~5 mm before the tread
centre at 3° of roll, so blend_envelope handed smooth road to the sweep, whose GJK rim
witness on the ground slab is loose. ground::discount_tilt removes the tilt's own lift
(half_width·|axle·n| / |dir·n|) before blending: the exact centre ray wins on smooth road,
kerbs still lift the sweep.

- tests/probe_chatter.rs: 953 N → < 60 N RMS (rampart_50, shiro_turbo, kestrel_ts);
  straight 0; load transfer kept. Vehicle::wheel_loads() for it.
- [bless] simcli goldens: the 64 the fix changes (64 hashes.txt + 8 replays); all 109
  green before (round12 b5fcfcf8) and after.
- [bless] slide_control wheel_profile hashes (a ground-contact change, not slide code).
- simcli run: all expected ranges pass; cargo test -p wp_vehicle / -p wp_wasm pass;
  clippy, lint-determinism, wasm build clean.

Found on lead/grip-balance (docs/integration/grip-balance.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FKfdoiNS5WT1M85cD1WAu9
